    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq",
      "url": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq",
      "inLanguage": "en-AU",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#webpage"
      },
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q1",
          "name": "What are the benefits?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q1-a",
            "text": "Help streamline decision-making if suspected infringement occurs.\n May help you build clear evidence of ownership that deters copycats.\n May help secure investment by demonstrating due diligence on IP.\n May support expansion into new markets or product lines.\n- Assist your employees and partners in developing team awareness on how to handle ideas and branding."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q2",
          "name": "What are the risks?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q2-a",
            "text": "Plans can become outdated if not reviewed regularly, leaving blind spots.\n Over-protection (for example, filing unnecessary patents) may waste resources.\n- Relying on internal resources rather than expert input may create false confidence."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q3",
          "name": "What are the possible outcomes?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q3-a",
            "text": "Developing a comprehensive IP strategy may not immediately yield a tangible outcome. This option involves preparation and implementation of preventative measures."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q4",
          "name": "What might the costs be?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q4-a",
            "text": "Creating an IP strategy in-house can be free apart from staff time. For example, it may take a few days to compile an inventory and action list. Engaging an IP professional such as IP lawyers, IP attorneys, or IP commercialisation experts for a tailored plan would involve professional fees, which may vary depending on the scale and complexity of the plan.  \n\nOngoing costs, however, relate mainly to the protection steps you choose, such as renewal fees or monitoring services."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q5",
          "name": "How much time might be involved?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q5-a",
            "text": "Drafting a simple strategy may take around a day or two of focused work. More detailed plans that cover multiple IP types and overseas markets may take several weeks to months, especially if you seek professional advice. \n\nAlso, consider reviewing the strategy at least annually, or whenever you launch new products or enter new markets."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q6",
          "name": "How much is this used?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q6-a",
            "text": "Developing and implementing a comprehensive IP strategy a common practice used by businesses that own or use multiple IP assets."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q7",
          "name": "Who can use this?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q7-a",
            "text": "IP rights holders or authorised users managing IP assets.\n Anyone or businesses planning to use, develop or acquire IP assets."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q8",
          "name": "Who's involved?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q8-a",
            "text": "The business owner or employee/s.\n Optional: IP professionals such as trade mark or patent attorneys.\n- Optional: Business advisors or accountants assisting with commercial planning."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q9",
          "name": "What do you need to proceed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://ipfirstresponse.ipaustralia.gov.au/options/develop-strategy-manage-your-ip#faq-q9-a",
            "text": "IP strategies can vary in its scope and complexity depending on a wide range of factors such as the number of IP assets involved, the size of your business and the composition of your IP portfolio. While businesses can take many different approaches in designing their IP strategies, a common starting point is conducting an IP audit to create a clear register of IP assets owned and used by your business."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
